# Who may use in-game chat commands through the GM bridge (libexec/dune-gm-bridge; docs/admin.md, "In-game chat
# commands"). Save as gm_bridge.conf in the config directory (chmod 600). Read for every command, so edits apply at once.
#
# One line per player:   <character name or FLS id>: <command> <command>...
# or, for every command: <character name or FLS id>: *
# Commands: where goto bring say timeout give give-others kick. Anyone listed may also use help.
# give puts items into your own inventory; give-others into another (online) player's. `*` grants every command.
# A 16-hex-digit entry is an FLS id (dune-awakening character whois <id> names it) and matches that account only;
# anything else is a character name, matched exactly. Nobody listed, or no file, means nobody may use the bridge.
#
#Alice: *
#0123456789ABCDEF: where goto bring give
